    "content": "<p class=\"ref-note\">Model, K-factor and Sprinkler Identification Number (SIN) for the Tyco Peak Performance attic sprinklers. The TY prefix is a redesignation of the older C prefix (for example, TY4180 was C4180). Finish is natural brass. Listed by UL and C-UL for the service shown in the design criteria only.</p><div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table><tr><th>Model</th><th>K</th><th>SIN</th><th>Inlet (NPT)</th><th>Temperature</th><th>Operating element</th><th>Part number</th></tr><tr><td>BB1</td><td>8.0</td><td>TY4180</td><td>3/4 in</td><td>200°F (93°C)</td><td>Glass bulb</td><td>51-623-1-200</td></tr><tr><td>BB2</td><td>8.0</td><td>TY4181</td><td>3/4 in</td><td>200°F (93°C)</td><td>Glass bulb</td><td>51-621-1-200</td></tr><tr><td>BB3</td><td>8.0</td><td>TY4182</td><td>3/4 in</td><td>200°F (93°C)</td><td>Glass bulb</td><td>51-622-1-200</td></tr><tr><td>BB1</td><td>5.6</td><td>TY3180</td><td>1/2 in</td><td>212°F (100°C)</td><td>Fusible link</td><td>50-601-1-212</td></tr><tr><td>BB2</td><td>5.6</td><td>TY3181</td><td>1/2 in</td><td>212°F (100°C)</td><td>Fusible link</td><td>50-602-1-212</td></tr><tr><td>BB3</td><td>5.6</td><td>TY3182</td><td>1/2 in</td><td>212°F (100°C)</td><td>Fusible link</td><td>50-603-1-212</td></tr><tr><td>BB1</td><td>4.2</td><td>TY2180</td><td>1/2 in</td><td>200°F (93°C)</td><td>Glass bulb</td><td>50-620-1-200</td></tr><tr><td>BB2</td><td>4.2</td><td>TY2181</td><td>1/2 in</td><td>200°F (93°C)</td><td>Glass bulb</td><td>50-621-1-200</td></tr><tr><td>BB3</td><td>4.2</td><td>TY2182</td><td>1/2 in</td><td>200°F (93°C)</td><td>Glass bulb</td><td>50-622-1-200</td></tr><tr><td>SD1</td><td>5.6</td><td>TY3183</td><td>1/2 in</td><td>212°F (100°C)</td><td>Fusible link</td><td>50-611-1-212</td></tr><tr><td>SD2</td><td>5.6</td><td>TY3184</td><td>1/2 in</td><td>212°F (100°C)</td><td>Fusible link</td><td>50-612-1-212</td></tr><tr><td>SD3</td><td>5.6</td><td>TY3185</td><td>1/2 in</td><td>212°F (100°C)</td><td>Fusible link</td><td>50-613-1-212</td></tr><tr><td>HIP</td><td>5.6</td><td>TY3187</td><td>1/2 in</td><td>200°F (93°C)</td><td>Glass bulb</td><td>51-620-1-200</td></tr><tr><td>AP</td><td>5.6</td><td>TY3190</td><td>1/2 in</td><td>200°F (93°C)</td><td>Glass bulb</td><td>50-625-1-200</td></tr><tr><td>AP</td><td>4.2</td><td>TY2190</td><td>1/2 in</td><td>200°F (93°C)</td><td>Glass bulb</td><td>50-624-1-200</td></tr></table></div><p class=\"ref-note\" style=\"margin-top:10px\">Model key: BB = Back to Back (dual directional), SD = Single Directional, HIP = hip roof, AP = Attic Plus (combustible concealed space sprinkler). Suffix 1, 2, 3 = roof pitch version (see Table A).</p><p class=\"ref-note\">Installation: use the correct sprinkler wrench on the wrench flats or wrench hex only, never the deflector. Torque is 7 to 14 ft-lb for a 1/2 in NPT joint and 10 to 20 ft-lb for a 3/4 in NPT joint. Do not install a bulb sprinkler with a cracked bulb or lost liquid.</p><div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table><tr><th>Sprinkler</th><th>Wrench</th><th>Part number</th></tr><tr><td>BB K=8.0</td><td>W-Type 3</td><td>56-895-1-001</td></tr><tr><td>BB K=4.2 and AP (K=4.2 and 5.6)</td><td>W-Type 6</td><td>56-000-6-387</td></tr><tr><td>HIP K=5.6</td><td>W-Type 20</td><td>56-000-1-106</td></tr><tr><td>BB K=5.6 and SD K=5.6</td><td>Adjustable wrench on wrench hex</td><td>—</td></tr></table></div>",
