    "content": "<p class=\"ref-note\">Table A from TFP610: allowable roof span, minimum flow and pressure, and roof pitch. Roof pitch is rise over run. There is no interpolation: round every case up to the next higher span. Example: a 45 ft span with a BB1 (K=8.0) is calculated as 60 ft.</p><div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table><tr><th>Model</th><th>K</th><th>SIN</th><th>Allowable roof span, ft</th><th>Minimum flow, gpm (lpm)</th><th>Minimum pressure, psi (bar)</th><th>Roof pitch (rise over run)</th></tr><tr><td>BB1</td><td>8.0</td><td>TY4180</td><td>≤ 60 (18.3 m)</td><td>38 (144)</td><td>22.6 (1.5)</td><td>4:12 to less than 7:12</td></tr><tr><td>BB2</td><td>8.0</td><td>TY4181</td><td>≤ 60 (18.3 m)</td><td>38 (144)</td><td>22.6 (1.5)</td><td>7:12 to less than 10:12</td></tr><tr><td>BB3</td><td>8.0</td><td>TY4182</td><td>≤ 60 (18.3 m)</td><td>40 (152)</td><td>25.0 (1.7)</td><td>10:12 to 12:12</td></tr><tr><td>BB1 / BB2 / BB3</td><td>5.6</td><td>TY3180 / 3181 / 3182</td><td>over 40 (12.2 m) to 60 (18.3 m)</td><td>38 (144)</td><td>46.0 (3.2)</td><td>BB1 4:12 to less than 7:12; BB2 7:12 to less than 10:12; BB3 10:12 to 12:12</td></tr><tr><td>BB1 / BB2 / BB3</td><td>5.6</td><td>TY3180 / 3181 / 3182</td><td>≤ 40 (12.2 m)</td><td>25 (95)</td><td>20.0 (1.4)</td><td>Same as above</td></tr><tr><td>BB1 / BB2 / BB3</td><td>4.2</td><td>TY2180 / 2181 / 2182</td><td>≤ 20 (6.1 m)</td><td>13 (49)</td><td>9.6 (0.7)</td><td>BB1 3:12 to less than 7:12; BB2 7:12 to less than 10:12; BB3 10:12 to 12:12</td></tr><tr><td>SD1 / SD2 / SD3</td><td>5.6</td><td>TY3183 / 3184 / 3185</td><td>over 30 (9.1 m) to 40 (12.2 m)</td><td>35 (132)</td><td>39.0 (2.7)</td><td>SD1 4:12 to less than 7:12; SD2 7:12 to less than 10:12; SD3 10:12 to 12:12</td></tr><tr><td>SD1 / SD2 / SD3</td><td>5.6</td><td>TY3183 / 3184 / 3185</td><td>over 10 (3.0 m) to 30 (9.1 m)</td><td>25 (95)</td><td>20.0 (1.4)</td><td>Same as above</td></tr><tr><td>SD1 / SD2 / SD3</td><td>5.6</td><td>TY3183 / 3184 / 3185</td><td>≤ 10 (3.0 m)</td><td>19 (72)</td><td>11.5 (0.8)</td><td>Same as above</td></tr><tr><td>HIP</td><td>5.6</td><td>TY3187</td><td>over 20 (6.1 m) to 28 (8.5 m)</td><td>34 (129)</td><td>36.9 (2.5)</td><td>4:12 to 12:12</td></tr><tr><td>HIP</td><td>5.6</td><td>TY3187</td><td>≤ 20 (6.1 m)</td><td>25 (95)</td><td>20.0 (1.4)</td><td>4:12 to 12:12</td></tr><tr><td>AP</td><td>5.6</td><td>TY3190</td><td>10 ft x 12 ft (3.1 m x 3.6 m), see note (e)</td><td>7 psi (0.48 bar) minimum</td><td>0.10 gpm/sq ft (4.1 mm/min) design density</td><td>3:12 to 12:12</td></tr><tr><td>AP</td><td>4.2</td><td>TY2190</td><td>10 ft x 12 ft (3.1 m x 3.6 m), see note (e)</td><td>7 psi (0.48 bar) minimum</td><td>0.10 gpm/sq ft (4.1 mm/min) design density</td><td>3:12 to 12:12</td></tr></table></div><p class=\"ref-note\" style=\"margin-top:10px\">Notes: BB and SD roof span is measured horizontally. HIP roof span is measured as shown in Figure 12 of the data sheet. AP roof span is measured along the slope, up to 10 ft perpendicular to the slope by 12 ft parallel to it. Dry pipe maximum water delivery time: 45 seconds for BB K=4.2, 60 seconds for AP, otherwise refer to NFPA 13 (2007 edition) section 7.2.3.</p><p class=\"ref-note\">Key design limits: light hazard only. Wet system using CPVC or steel pipe, or dry system using steel pipe. Attics over 80 ft (24.4 m) wide cannot use attic sprinklers.</p><div class=\"tbl-scroll\"><table><tr><th>Item</th><th>Limit</th></tr><tr><td>Spacing along branch line, BB and SD</td><td>4 ft (1.2 m) minimum, 6 ft (1.8 m) maximum on center</td></tr><tr><td>Spacing along branch line, HIP</td><td>3 ft (0.9 m) minimum, 6 ft (1.8 m) maximum on center</td></tr><tr><td>Spacing, AP</td><td>7 ft (2.1 m) minimum along the branch line; 10 ft (3.1 m) maximum perpendicular to slope and 12 ft (3.6 m) maximum parallel to slope</td></tr><tr><td>BB, SD or HIP to standard spray sprinkler</td><td>6 ft (1.8 m) along the peak or ridge; 26 ft (7.9 m) in the slope direction</td></tr><tr><td>AP to standard spray sprinkler</td><td>7 ft (2.1 m) along the peak or ridge</td></tr><tr><td>Deflector below peak, pitch 4:12 to 12:12</td><td>16 in (406 mm) minimum to 22 in (559 mm) maximum</td></tr><tr><td>Deflector below peak, pitch 3:12 to 4:12</td><td>12 in (305 mm) maximum below the peak and 1 in (25 mm) minimum below the bottom of the top chord or solid rafter</td></tr><tr><td>AP deflector position</td><td>1 to 3 in (25 to 76 mm) below the bottom of the top chord or solid rafter; deflector parallel to roof</td></tr><tr><td>Distance from trusses</td><td>6 in (152 mm) minimum from the face of the truss</td></tr><tr><td>BB or HIP from ridge centerline</td><td>6 in (152 mm) maximum</td></tr><tr><td>Above scissor truss, BB or SD</td><td>18 in (457 mm) minimum</td></tr><tr><td>SD at shear wall or draft curtain</td><td>4 to 6 in (102 to 152 mm) from the face and 8 in (203 mm) minimum above the bottom of the draft curtain</td></tr><tr><td>Orientation</td><td>BB and SD upright with flow arrows pointing down the slope; HIP with deflector parallel to the slope and flow arrows pointing down the two opposing slopes; AP upright with deflector parallel to the roof slope</td></tr></table></div>",
